# Pixel art and captures are binary.
#
# Git's content sniffing happens to classify these correctly today --
# every icon has a NUL byte within its first 8000 bytes, so it is left
# alone. But a bright icon with no NUL that early would be treated as
# text and CRLF-mangled by a Windows checkout, corrupting that one icon
# in Windows builds only and nowhere else. Say it outright instead.
*.ppm binary
*.png binary
*.gbc binary
*.gb  binary
*.sav binary
*.pam binary
